# Per-run E2E artefacts (scripts/run-openbw-e2e.sh writes _AI/e2e/runs/<stamp>_<tier>/).
# The raw logs and server output are per-run bulk and belong to the run, not the repo;
# the verdict tables that SUMMARISE them do belong (see _AI/e2e/README.md). run.txt is
# kept because it is the run's identity: map, tier, jar and the expectations that were
# asserted, which is what a later reader needs to reproduce or trust a table entry.
/_AI/e2e/runs/*/bot.log
/_AI/e2e/runs/*/server.log
/_AI/e2e/runs/latest
_AI/e2e/runs/20*